## Why This Is Asked
Tests SwiftUI, Combine, and simple disk persistence in a beginner-friendly way, plus lifecycle handling.

## Key Concepts
- SwiftUI state management and data binding
- Combine debounce to throttle rapid changes
- Lightweight persistence to disk (Documents) with Codable or plain text
- Lifecycle considerations (background/foreground)

## Code Example
```swift
import SwiftUI
import Combine

class NoteViewModel: ObservableObject {
  @Published var text: String = ""
  @Published var wordCount: Int = 0

  private var cancellables = Set<AnyCancellable>()

  init() {
    $text
      .debounce(for: .milliseconds(300), scheduler: RunLoop.main)
      .map { $0.split(whereSeparator: { $0 == " " || $0 == "\n" }).count }
      .assign(to: \.wordCount, on: self)
      .store(in: &cancellables)
  }

  func saveToDisk() {
    // write to Documents/notes.txt
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test that debounce correctly throttles rapid input?
- How would you handle a save failure and retry strategy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests CRDT knowledge, offline collaboration, and practical data modeling for cross-device sync. It also evaluates how to bound growth, ensure deterministic reconciliation, and integrate with a common iOS stack.

## Key Concepts
- CRDTs: OR-Set for attachments, observed-remove with vector clocks for changes
- Append-only logs and per-Asset clocks
- Deterministic reconciliation on reconnect
- Realm/SQLite as storage backends
- Lightweight conflict resolver and delta generation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple OR-Set merge sketch (JS for illustration)
function mergeORSet(localAdds, remoteAdds, localRemoves, remoteRemoves) {
  const adds = new Set([...localAdds, ...remoteAdds]);
  const removes = new Set([...localRemoves, ...remoteRemoves]);
  return Array.from(adds).filter(x => !removes.has(x));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test concurrency and network partitions affecting reconciliation?
- How would you prune historical data without breaking causality remediation?
